'''Pets''' are [[Non-Playable-Character|NPCs]] who spawn and despawn at your command and who follow you around in the game world. Pets are permanent objects that can be used and reused without a cool down timer. They do not appear in your inventory and cannot be sold or traded. You may have duplicates of pets, but only one pet may be in play at a time.

Pets provide a number of benefits. When you have a happy pet in play it provides you with a speed boost. Pets locate and dig up treasure chests, and the only way to complete the Springs collections<ref>The Springs collections are the following collections: [[Bouncy Metal Springs]], [[Golden Metal Springs]], [[Oiled Metal Springs]], and [[Tightly Coiled Metal Springs]]</ref> is by opening treasure chests. They have thought bubbles that notify you when you are near a [[Battles|battle]]/[[Dungeons|dungeon]] or a [[Collections|collection]] spawn. Pets perform tricks. Cats and dogs can wear clothes and costumes. Pets appear in your [[:Category:Lots|housing lots]] to run around in random fashion. Pets can be renamed by selecting names off of premade name lists.

Pets have requirements to be kept happy. Each pet has their own set of status bars: one for hunger, one for cleanliness, and one for entertainment. While these bars are high your pet will be happy and will provide you with a speed boost. They will also have happy thoughts and visibly appear happy. While these bars are low your pet will be unhappy and will not provide you with a speed boost. They will have sad thoughts and will visibly appear sad. All three status bars will slowly decrease while your pet goes unused and all three bars will quickly decrease while your pet is in use. For more information about maintaining a pet, see [[Pet Care]].

Pets are mainly sold in the [[Station Cash Marketplace|SC Marketplace]], under the Pets category. There are a few pets available from other means though, and there are some pets that were sold for a limited time only.

To use your pet, click on the paw icon in the [[User Interface]] and select a pet from the menu that appears. To remove your pet, locate its information in the upper-right-hand side of the User Interface and click on the X icon. You may not use a pet while in a [[Mini-Games|minigame]], dungeon, or duel, although upon exiting the minigame the pet will still be spawned. For more information how to use pets, see [[Pet Interface]].

